menu "lastDSMRlogger P1 Interface"

    choice LASTDSMRLOGGER_P1_RX_POLARITY
        prompt "P1 RX signal polarity"
        default LASTDSMRLOGGER_P1_RX_DIRECT
        help
            Select how the chosen P1 interface presents the meter signal to
            the ESP32-S3. The smart meter P1 port always connects to UART0:
            RX on GPIO44, TX on GPIO43. The smart meter P1 port is an
            idle-high interface. Use the setting documented for the
            interface board; the selection is fixed at build time.

        config LASTDSMRLOGGER_P1_RX_DIRECT
            bool "Direct (non-inverted) signal from the P1 interface"

        config LASTDSMRLOGGER_P1_RX_INVERTED
            bool "Inverted signal (interface inverts before the ESP32-S3)"
    endchoice

    comment "The P1 request signal is externally enabled in this release."

endmenu
